{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1795154167580273002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"neglectful-acceptable-gerbil","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"bad6c398b89de9339e6c2c0fc935a96afc6d3442c9e17750616c33c1ad91a626","event_uuid":"ed4728e2-e3e5-4ecf-be7f-71867ad5689d","position":{"commit_sha":"88c03b314c52b249a5edd9254c17585f24f61baa","position":"1795154110807042001-ed4728e2-e3e5-4ecf-be7f-71867ad5689d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"7157d69be559ecd6f313e059d88204f2245801bcfbddcec08214d995830e81fd","event_uuid":"7e61bfee-7b82-4cd4-9bb7-aa57779e2b9f","position":{"commit_sha":"aed54b0e0a1bf02531b4f55e7f2cc6d725cdc736","position":"1795154135411632001-7e61bfee-7b82-4cd4-9bb7-aa57779e2b9f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"c1ab14eb51399c94bd50870059750eb402aae0f21da65044916e5726056d749b","event_uuid":"5bd27674-8694-4987-b49f-2383258dbbca","position":{"commit_sha":"31e3ca529642bbadb4235f4d84bdd00c7f375260","position":"1795154167580273001-5bd27674-8694-4987-b49f-2383258dbbca"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795154110807042001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7e61bfee-7b82-4cd4-9bb7-aa57779e2b9f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"8aa0-2120-5ef3-4750"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff, which owns `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`. These 11 entries move to `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/crlf.args`, which this bug owns.\n\nThe runner's system gitconfig sets `core.autocrlf=true` (diagnostic run 44672240702, step \"Show git config\": `file:C:/Program Files/Git/etc/gitconfig core.autocrlf=true`). Vendored files not pinned `eol=lf` check out with CRLF, so their pinned SHA-256 no longer matches (`test_jira_dc_harness_shape.py`, `test_bridge_provider_wrappers.py`, `test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py`). Text-mode writes and stdin add `\\r`: the plan-replay `objects/info/alternates` path reads back as `objects?` (`test_plan_replay_tier2.py`), `run_git` text stdin hashes differently (`test_run_git_wrapper.py::test_str_input_is_forwarded_to_stdin`), and `sha256sum` sees `'mcp-publisher.tar.gz'$'\\r'` (`test_mcp_publisher_pin.py`). On macOS, `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` with `core.autocrlf=true` reproduces `test_dc_store_copy_bounded_25e0.py` and `test_reclaim_bridge_history.py`.\n\nEvidence: Windows runs on throwaway branch `tmp/w05-remeasure` with origin/main `717c50f8b33` code plus a selection-only workflow change: run 44665461131 (the 242 `unclassified.args` entries; 48 passed, 194 failed or errored) and run 44681457334 (the 194, xdist, JUnit XML with full tracebacks). Both 2026-11-19 PST.\n\nModules:\n- `tests/integration/test_reclaim_bridge_history.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier2.py` (4)\n- `tests/unit/reconciler/test_jira_dc_harness_shape.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_dc_store_copy_bounded_25e0.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_mcp_publisher_pin.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/test_run_git_wrapper.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_bridge_provider_wrappers.py` (1)\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_reconcile_workflow_lint.py` (1)\n\n## Approach\nPin the vendored and hashed files `eol=lf` in `.gitattributes`, write LF explicitly where a file or stdin feeds git or a checksum, and decide whether rebar's own git calls pin `core.autocrlf=false` for the tickets store. Remove each line from `crlf.args` as it passes.\n\n## Scope\nTest or product code for the listed modules, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/crlf.args` (remove each fixed line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every line removed from `crlf.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `crlf.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason.\n","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":".github/windows-sweep-deselect/crlf.args","reason":"remove each line as its test is fixed"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"51c6-9f1d-595b-411f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: 11 tests fail on CRLF from core.autocrlf=true or text-mode newline translation","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["ed4728e2-e3e5-4ecf-be7f-71867ad5689d","7e61bfee-7b82-4cd4-9bb7-aa57779e2b9f","5bd27674-8694-4987-b49f-2383258dbbca"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795154167580273002,"uuid":"838ad651-d373-49ea-b448-f72811782d40"}
